## Claim
Text: "China seek for court’s approval to kill the over 20,000 coronavirus patients to avoid further spread of the virus."
Claim author: City News
Claim date: October 08, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did any official Chinese government body or representative formally petition a court for legal authorization to execute individuals diagnosed with COVID-19 in October 2020?
Answer: No, the claim is false. According to a VERA Files fact-check, the story originated from disreputable websites and was "fake and baseless," with no record of such a petition in China's Supreme People’s Court or official government channels.

Source URL: https://verafiles.org/articles/vera-files-fact-check-report-claiming-china-kill-20k-covid-1

### Is there any official record, court document, or credible journalistic report from October 2020 that details a request by Chinese authorities for judicial approval to kill over 20,000 coronavirus patients?
Answer: Based on the search result's fact-check analysis, there is no official record, court document, or credible journalistic report from October 2020 detailing such a request. The claim originates from a non-credible website known for publishing fake news, and "not a single credible media house across the globe has reported this news." The official website of China's Supreme People's Court contains no such case particulars.

Source URL: https://archive.siasat.com/news/fact-check-did-china-sought-approval-kill-20000-patients-1818719/

### What is the established identity, credibility, and publication history of the news outlet "City News" that originally published this claim on October 8, 2020?
Answer: Based on the Snopes investigation, "City News" (also known as AB-TC) is not a credible news source; it has a documented history of publishing hoaxes, misinformation, and false articles—including previous debunked stories about coronavirus—while providing no author bylines or supporting evidence for its claims. As Snopes states, "this website doesn't exactly have a great track record of genuine news reporting," and it was even corrected by the Singapore government for publishing coronavirus falsehoods.

Source URL: https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/china-kill-coronavirus-patients/

